# Who gets asked to look at a change.
# ============================================================================
#
# GitHub reads this file from the default branch and requests a review from
# everyone it names whose paths a pull request touches. One rule, covering
# everything, because this repository has two people in it and both of them
# care about all of it — a path-by-path split would be inventing a division of
# labour that does not exist.
#
# An author is never asked to review their own pull request, so in practice
# this means each of us is asked to look at the other's work, automatically,
# without anyone having to remember to add a reviewer.
#
# ## Requested, not required
#
# `main`'s protection asks for one approving review and does not care whose,
# so this file schedules the ask rather than gating the merge. That is
# deliberate: a rule that *required* a code owner would block whichever of us
# is working while the other is asleep, in a two-person repository across time
# zones. The owner keeps an admin bypass either way.
#
# If that ever stops being the right trade — a third contributor, an outside
# pull request that must not merge on one person's say-so — the switch is
# `require_code_owner_reviews` on the branch protection, not a change here.
#
# ## On this repository, the asking is done by a workflow
#
# GitHub requests these reviews itself on a repository owned by an
# organisation. It does not here — this one is owned by a person, the
# `codeowners/errors` API answers 404 for this file, and a pull request opened
# with it in place drew no request at all (checked 2026-08-31). So the ask is
# performed by `.github/workflows/request-review.yml`, and this file stays as
# the declaration of who the owners are — correct today, and load-bearing the
# day this repository moves into an org.
#
# ## Everyone named here needs write access
#
# GitHub silently ignores a code owner who cannot push to the repository: no
# request is made, no error is shown, and the file simply appears not to work.
# If a reviewer stops being asked, check their collaborator status first.

